# RS-VIEW (PR 318) at the 512 MiB floor: `cview -d` decodes a 3840 x 2160 PNG to the digest of its pixels (sh/view.sh,
# status 0); then View opens it in a window, which takes the large buffers (guest.py color reads its middle); q ends it.
hdesk: screen 1920x1080 plane 1920x
=hdesk: terminal 1 ended, status 0
~hdesk: float 1 app -?[0-9]+ frame -?[0-9]+,-?[0-9]+ [0-9]+x[0-9]+
~hdesk: pixel 1 pid [0-9]+ size [0-9]+x[0-9]+
=hdesk: pixel 1 ended
=hdesk: shell ended, status 0
!fault: cint-core-1/fault/v2
